In-Reply-To: <nIawGEgoMGo.n7jgu1QACwAJ@cardinalmsi.groups.google.com>
References: <nIawGEgoMGo.n7jgu1QACwAJ@cardinalmsi.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/cardinalmsi/c/nIawGEgoMGo/m/UIMhGI8HCwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Nivedita,

That means that you're trying to import 'processed' imzML data with recorded m/z values that are 0 or negative. This makes it impossible calculate bin widths based on ppm. Use units.accuracy="mz", and set your desired bin width using the mass.accuracy parameter.

-Kylie

